Unless you have a +7 all-around artifact weapon and maxed combat skills
for it, you're also lacking reflection or magic resistance, and you're
willing to cope with "You feel restrained in this armour -more-" every
time you attack, don't wear silver or grey dragon scale mail.

Any other body armour shouldn't be considered at all, period.

(My current character on NAO is a monk. He has no reflection (SoR
hinders casting; AoLS is more useful) and maxed skills in his +7 Vorpal
Blade. He still isn't wearing any body armor, despite being level 30,
on move 80000, and having cleared out the entire dungeon.)



